The Ten Commandments in a new interpretation for the present time by Abd-ru-shin, the author of the Grail Message - In the Light of Truth. The interpretations are reproduced in the original, uncommented and unabridged.


The 10th Commandment:


You shall not covet your neighbor’s house, his property, his cattle, or anything that belongs to him!


Anyone who seeks to make a profit through honest work and honest trade can wait calmly for the call of this commandment at the great reckoning; for it will pass him by without striking him hard. It is actually so easy to fulfil all the commandments, and yet... just take a good look at all people , and you will soon come to the realisation that even this observance of the commandment, which is actually quite natural for people, does not happen or only very rarely, and then not with joy, but only with great effort.


Like an insatiable desire, it rages over all people, whether white, yellow, brown, black or red, to envy other people for what they themselves do not possess. Or, to put it even better: to envy them everything! In this envy also lies the forbidden desire! The transgression of the commandment is thus already complete and becomes the root of many evils that quickly cause people to fall, from which they often never rise again.


Strangely enough, the average person rarely values ​​what he calls his own, but only what he does not yet possess. The darkness diligently spread desire, and unfortunately human souls gave themselves up all too willingly in order to create the most fertile soil for the sad seed.


As time went on, the desire for other people's possessions became the basis for everything that most people did. It started with a simple wish, progressed through cunning and the art of persuasion to limitless envy, constant dissatisfaction and blind hatred.


Any path to satisfaction was recognized as justifiable, as long as it did not conflict too obviously with earthly laws. God's command was ignored in the growing desire for gain! Everyone believed that he was truly honorable as long as he was not called to account by the earthly court. But it did not cost him much effort to avoid this, for he applied the greatest caution and the sharpest intelligence when it was his intention to ruthlessly harm his fellow human beings as soon as it became necessary in order to gain some kind of cheap advantage.


He did not think that in reality this would cost him much more than all the earthly means could help him with! So-called cleverness became the trump card! However, cleverness according to today's concepts is nothing more than the flower of cunning or an increase of it. It is just strange that everyone distrusts the clever person, but respects the wise one! The general basic attitude gives rise to absurdity.


The clever man is a bungler in the art of satisfying his desires, while intelligent people are masters at it. The bungler cannot clothe his desires in beautiful forms and only earns pitying contempt for this. But the expert receives the most envious admiration from souls who share the same inclination!


Here too there is envy, because in the context of modern humanity even admiration of the same kind cannot be without envy. People do not know this strong driving force behind the many evils; they no longer know that this envy in many forms currently dominates and guides all their thoughts and actions! It is present in individuals as well as in entire nations, it controls states, gives rise to wars as well as parties and eternal strife when only two people have something to discuss!


Where is obedience to the tenth commandment of God, one would like to warn the states! In the most merciless desire, each of the earthly states strives only to possess the other! They do not shy away from individual murder, not even from mass murder, not from enslaving entire peoples, just to elevate themselves to greatness. The fine speeches about self-preservation or self-protection are only excuses, because they themselves clearly feel that something must be said to mitigate or excuse these monstrous crimes against the commandments of God!


But it is of no use to them; for the pen that engraves the disregard of God's commandments in the book of world events is inexorable, and the threads of karma that are tied to each individual are unbreakable, so that not even the smallest stirring of his thoughts and actions can be lost without being solved!


Anyone who can see all these threads can see what a terrible judgment has now been brought about! Confusion and the collapse of what has been built up so far are only the first slight consequences of this most shameful of violations of the tenth commandment of God! No one can be merciful to you as soon as the full consequences begin to break over you more and more. You deserve nothing else. What will come is only what you have forced upon yourselves!


Tear the impure desires completely out of your soul! Remember that a state is also made up of individuals! Give up all envy and hatred towards people who, in your opinion, have much more than you! There is a reason for this! But you alone are to blame for the fact that you are not able to recognize the reason, since you have voluntarily imposed on yourself the enormous and God- unwilling restriction of your ability to understand, which must appear as the result of your unfortunate servility to reason!


Anyone who is not satisfied with the position given to him in the new kingdom of God here on earth through the effects of his own karma threads, is not worthy of living in it! Not worthy of being given the opportunity to relatively easily resolve old debts that are hanging over him and at the same time to mature spiritually in order to find the way up to the home of all free spirits, where only light and joy reign!


In the future, every dissatisfied person will be mercilessly swept away as a useless disturber of the peace that is finally desired, as an obstacle to healthy ascent! But if there is still a good seed in him, which strongly guarantees a speedy change, he will come to the realization of the absolute rightness of God's wise will; rightness even for him who until now could not recognize, only out of the short-sightedness of his soul and out of self-inflicted stupidity, that the bed in which he now lies on earth was made by him alone for himself as an unconditional consequence of his entire existence up to now, several lives in the afterlife and also on earth, and is not the blind arbitrary act of chance!


He will finally realize that he needs for himself precisely that and only that which he has experienced and where he stands, including the circumstances into which he was born and everything that comes with it!


If he works diligently on himself, he will not only rise spiritually but also on earth. However, if he defiantly wants to force himself to take a different path, ruthlessly and to the detriment of his fellow human beings, this can never be of any real benefit to him.


It will be a hard struggle for human souls before they can break free from their habitual transgressions of God's tenth commandment, that is, change in it, and finally live by it in thought, speech and deed! But for all those who cannot do this, suffering and destruction await here on earth and in the afterlife!


